Bridge 0129: MSAA colour resolve by Turnip's own AVERAGE for 8-bit unorm. The runtime resolved every attachment whose
format has Metal's closed rule by its exact shader resolve after the pass (color_resolve.rs; a fullscreen draw per MSAA
pass, `13fc7332`, ~3.8 ms each in three.js games_fps, 2 a frame), because only MoltenVK has
DriverFact::ColorResolveAverageIsMetals. Now color_resolve::exact answers None for RGBA8Unorm/BGRA8Unorm at 2..4
samples, so the subpass keeps its resolve attachment (GMEM blit event, or the 2D engine in sysmem) and the image takes
no input attachment usage for it. Rounding: Metal (sum + n/2)/n over the codes, Turnip's integer average: at most
1 LSB apart (at a tie). sRGB stays exact unless mode 2: Turnip's GMEM blit averages sRGB codes, not linear values
(blit_can_resolve), up to ~60 LSB off at a black-white edge. Float/int/snorm/packed formats, >4 samples and the
sample-plane resolve (resolve_planes) unchanged. The runtime announces `device-rounded-resolve` once.
Logs `SWEET_M2V_HW_RESOLVE mode N` once per process (at its first multisampled 8-bit candidate).
Knob: SWEET_M2V_HW_RESOLVE (default 1 = unorm8; 0 = exact shader resolve as before; 2 = unorm8 and its sRGB formats).

